260
00:11:07,041 --> 00:11:09,294
PHOEBE:
You guys?

261
00:11:09,336 --> 00:11:10,504
Just a minute.

262
00:11:10,545 --> 00:11:12,589
That's Mrs. Tribbiani.

263
00:11:12,631 --> 00:11:15,091
You don't say anything.

264
00:11:15,133 --> 00:11:16,551
Why would I say anything?

265
00:11:16,593 --> 00:11:18,719
That two of our best friends
could start

266
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:20,847
the greatest love affair
of their lives

267
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:22,599
and they would have me to thank

268
00:11:22,641 --> 00:11:24,851
and then we could all start
having babies?

269
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:27,437
I'm not going
to let you say anything.

270
00:11:27,479 --> 00:11:29,272
You just stay here.

271
00:11:29,314 --> 00:11:31,650
Oh, God!

272
00:11:34,611 --> 00:11:37,489
Oh, hey, Monica,
I brought back your iron.

273
00:11:37,531 --> 00:11:39,407
Oh, you had that?
I thought I lost it.

274
00:11:39,449 --> 00:11:41,242
I got a new one,
like, a month ago.

275
00:11:41,284 --> 00:11:43,537
Oh, just as well.
I broke this one.

276
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:50,210
What?

277
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:51,252
Nothing.

278
00:11:51,294 --> 00:11:53,380
Okay.

279
00:11:53,421 --> 00:11:55,048
I mean, I really shouldn't say.

280
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:56,924
I mean, I'm really
not supposed to.

281
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:58,926
Fine.

282
00:11:58,968 --> 00:12:01,762
It's a humdinger.

283
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:05,016
Well, then it's really too bad
that you can't tell me.

284
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:06,476
Somebody likes you.

285
00:12:08,769 --> 00:12:10,355
( groans )

286
00:12:10,397 --> 00:12:12,190
Is it Chandler?

287
00:12:12,232 --> 00:12:14,484
No.

288
00:12:14,526 --> 00:12:16,570
Well, then tell him
to stop staring.

289
00:12:16,611 --> 00:12:18,905
It's Joey.

290
00:12:18,946 --> 00:12:21,241
Really? Joey?

291
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:23,826
You don't say.

292
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:25,620
Is it something
you'd be interested in?

293
00:12:25,662 --> 00:12:28,998
I don't know, I don't know,
I don't know.

294
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:30,749
You know, I mean,
on the one hand

295
00:12:30,791 --> 00:12:32,711
Mother, may I?

296
00:12:34,546 --> 00:12:37,382
But on the other hand...

297
00:12:37,424 --> 00:12:41,386
No. No, I can't.

298
00:12:41,428 --> 00:12:43,179
We're friends. No. Oh, no.

299
00:12:43,221 --> 00:12:45,390
I don't want to risk
what we have.

300
00:12:45,432 --> 00:12:48,309
I guess that makes sense.

301
00:12:48,351 --> 00:12:50,853
So, you think you're going
to talk to him?

302
00:12:50,895 --> 00:12:53,022
Sure, yeah.
I mean, it's Joey.

303
00:12:53,064 --> 00:12:55,191
I don't want him
to get hurt.

304
00:12:55,233 --> 00:12:57,527
Well, I must say
I am on fire.

305
00:12:57,569 --> 00:12:59,613
First Chandler, now Joey.

306
00:12:59,654 --> 00:13:02,781
No, no. Not Chandler,
just Joey.

307
00:13:02,823 --> 00:13:04,743
Sure.

308
00:13:12,459 --> 00:13:13,585
Hi.

309
00:13:13,627 --> 00:13:14,877
Hey.

310
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:16,546
You know what?
I've been thinking about it.

311
00:13:16,588 --> 00:13:18,423
I'm really coming around
on the name Ruth.

312
00:13:18,465 --> 00:13:20,883
I think I would actually
consider naming our child that.

313
00:13:20,925 --> 00:13:24,971
Rach, I can't tell you
how much that means to me.

314
00:13:25,012 --> 00:13:26,013
Oh...

315
00:13:28,391 --> 00:13:30,226
Wait a minute.

316
00:13:31,227 --> 00:13:32,312
Wait a minute.

317
00:13:32,353 --> 00:13:34,314
You-you hated the name Ruth.

318
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:37,358
Why... why would you
change your mind?

319
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:38,693
Unless...

320
00:13:38,735 --> 00:13:41,321
you know we're never
going to have to use it.

321
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:43,030
You did see the folder.

322
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:44,616
You know it's a boy!

323
00:13:44,658 --> 00:13:45,908
I didn't see anything.

324
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:48,077
I actually changed my mind
about the name.

325
00:13:48,119 --> 00:13:49,370
Oh, I don't think so.

326
00:13:49,412 --> 00:13:50,997
You're just giving me Ruth

327
00:13:51,038 --> 00:13:53,583
so you'll get to name
him when it's a boy.

328
00:13:53,625 --> 00:13:56,085
And then that's when
you'll swoop in

329
00:13:56,127 --> 00:13:57,420
and name him Heath

330
00:13:57,462 --> 00:14:00,799
or Blaine or... Sequoia.

331
00:14:00,839 --> 00:14:03,301
I would... Sequoia?

332
00:14:03,343 --> 00:14:04,302
Veto.

333
00:14:04,344 --> 00:14:06,053
Fine.

334
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:07,472
( laughs sarcastically )

335
00:14:07,514 --> 00:14:09,974
Unless...

336
00:14:10,016 --> 00:14:11,850
( groans )

337
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:15,605
you anticipated that
I would figure all this out

338
00:14:15,647 --> 00:14:17,940
and you know that it actually

339
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:19,442
is a girl, and...

340
00:14:19,484 --> 00:14:22,903
and you really do want
her to be named Ruth.

341
00:14:22,945 --> 00:14:25,906
Well, I'm not
falling for that!

342
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:28,785
Okay, Ruth is
off the table!

343
00:14:28,827 --> 00:14:31,705
But, Ross,
you want the name Ruth.

344
00:14:31,746 --> 00:14:33,373
Not like this.

345
00:14:36,083 --> 00:14:37,335
Hey.

346
00:14:37,377 --> 00:14:38,628
Hey.

347
00:14:38,670 --> 00:14:40,171
Well, what's up?

348
00:14:40,213 --> 00:14:42,674
Um, Joey, I know.

349
00:14:42,716 --> 00:14:44,425
What?

350
00:14:44,467 --> 00:14:47,345
I know.

351
00:14:47,387 --> 00:14:50,181
What...?

352
00:14:50,223 --> 00:14:52,517
I know about
your feelings.

353
00:14:52,559 --> 00:14:54,853
Oh, my God. You do?

354
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:56,270
Yes, and I'm sorry.

355
00:14:56,312 --> 00:14:58,981
I know things worked out
for Chandler and Monica

356
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:00,483
but that's very rare.

357
00:15:00,525 --> 00:15:01,651
I know, I know.

358
00:15:01,693 --> 00:15:04,028
And this is so much
more complicated

359
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:05,988
than it was for those guys.

360
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:08,324
I mean, it's Rachel,
for God sakes.

361
00:15:10,201 --> 00:15:14,205
For God sakes, it's Rachel!

362
00:15:14,247 --> 00:15:15,373
I know, I know.

363
00:15:15,415 --> 00:15:17,500
And she's not only
my friend

364
00:15:17,542 --> 00:15:19,502
she's my pregnant friend.

365
00:15:19,544 --> 00:15:21,880
She's my pregnant friend
who's Ross's ex.

366
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,465
Yeah, that's Rachel.

367
00:15:24,507 --> 00:15:26,175
Beat me over the head with it.

368
00:15:26,217 --> 00:15:30,012
What... what am
I going to do?

369
00:15:30,054 --> 00:15:31,431
You know, and I keep trying

370
00:15:31,472 --> 00:15:33,266
to get rid of these feelings,
you know?

371
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:34,893
I stayed up all last night

372
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:36,935
and made a list of everything
I don't like about her.

373
00:15:36,977 --> 00:15:38,354
You want to hear it?

374
00:15:38,396 --> 00:15:39,439
Yeah.

375
00:15:42,191 --> 00:15:44,985
She made me switch
to light mayo.

376
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:46,987
That's it! That's all I got!

377
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:48,907
And you know what?

378
00:15:48,948 --> 00:15:51,743
Tastes the same,
and my pants fit better.

379
00:15:51,785 --> 00:15:55,455
Joey, I think you're just
getting upset for nothing.

380
00:15:55,496 --> 00:15:57,331
This is probably just a crush.

381
00:15:57,373 --> 00:15:58,708
You think?

382
00:15:58,750 --> 00:16:00,251
Absolutely.

383
00:16:00,293 --> 00:16:02,044
You know, you get
this rush of feelings

384
00:16:02,086 --> 00:16:03,170
but then it goes away.

385
00:16:03,212 --> 00:16:04,589
Yeah, just a crush.

386
00:16:04,631 --> 00:16:06,090
That's all this is.

387
00:16:06,132 --> 00:16:07,425
It's a crush.

388
00:16:07,467 --> 00:16:10,136
I'm Joey. I don't
get deep feelings.

389
00:16:10,177 --> 00:16:11,888
That's right.
There you go.

390
00:16:11,930 --> 00:16:14,098
Yeah, crushes happen
all the time.

391
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:16,016
I know I've had them
for all you guys.

392
00:16:16,058 --> 00:16:17,852
Well, except
for Ross and Chandler.

393
00:16:17,894 --> 00:16:18,937
Well...

394
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:20,187
You know...

395
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:22,106
and I'm sure
you've had them for us.

396
00:16:22,148 --> 00:16:23,650
Not really.

397
00:16:23,691 --> 00:16:25,151
Mm-hmm.

398
00:16:25,192 --> 00:16:27,069
Throw me a bone here.

399
00:16:35,035 --> 00:16:39,540
So, I, uh... I
called the doctor

400
00:16:39,582 --> 00:16:43,127
and now we both know
the sex of the baby.

401
00:16:43,169 --> 00:16:45,254
What?
That's right.

402
00:16:45,296 --> 00:16:48,633
The student has
become the master.

403
00:16:48,675 --> 00:16:52,637
Ross, I swear, I don't know.

404
00:16:52,679 --> 00:16:54,806
Oh, come on, you
know it's a girl.

405
00:16:54,848 --> 00:16:56,432
A what?

406
00:16:56,474 --> 00:16:59,017
You... you really
didn't know?

407
00:16:59,059 --> 00:17:00,060
We're having a girl?

408
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:00,937
No.

409
00:17:00,979 --> 00:17:03,230
That's what you just said.

410
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:03,940
No.

411
00:17:03,982 --> 00:17:04,858
You said girl.

412
00:17:04,899 --> 00:17:06,985
Yes. I'm... I'm sorry.

413
00:17:07,025 --> 00:17:08,277
I'm so sorry.

414
00:17:08,319 --> 00:17:09,320
I'm not.

415
00:17:09,362 --> 00:17:10,738
We're having a girl!

416
00:17:10,780 --> 00:17:13,616
Sometimes I can't
believe it's with you.

417
00:17:13,658 --> 00:17:15,952
But still...
we're having a girl!

418
00:17:15,994 --> 00:17:17,954
Oh!
I know. I know.

419
00:17:17,996 --> 00:17:20,957
You know what?
I'm putting Ruth
back on the table.

420
00:17:20,999 --> 00:17:25,085
Oh... yes, we'll have ourselves
a little baby Ruth.

421
00:17:29,173 --> 00:17:30,383
Permission to veto.

422
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:32,176
Yes, please.

423
00:17:37,598 --> 00:17:39,141
Hey.

424
00:17:39,183 --> 00:17:41,644
Do I smell essential oils?

425
00:17:41,686 --> 00:17:42,937
Yeah, I'm going to take a bath.

426
00:17:42,979 --> 00:17:44,397
I was just going to get
a magazine.

427
00:17:44,438 --> 00:17:45,732
Okay.

428
00:18:01,372 --> 00:18:02,957
What do you think
you're doing?

429
00:18:04,918 --> 00:18:07,253
Leaving my troubles behind?

430
00:18:07,294 --> 00:18:09,422
All right, look, I know
that you're new at this

431
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:12,550
but this is completely
unacceptable bath decorum.

432
00:18:12,592 --> 00:18:16,387
Oh, it's so hard to care
when you're this relaxed.

433
00:18:16,429 --> 00:18:17,680
Okay, fine.

434
00:18:17,722 --> 00:18:19,015
You can have the bath

435
00:18:19,057 --> 00:18:20,641
but I am taking your boat.

436
00:18:20,683 --> 00:18:22,852
Now you're just a girl in a tub.

437
00:18:23,937 --> 00:18:25,772
Ooh... oh.

438
00:18:25,813 --> 00:18:26,689
Hey!

439
00:18:26,731 --> 00:18:28,441
Hi, Bubbles. Manly.

440
00:18:29,692 --> 00:18:31,027
Well, I just thought
I would drop by

441
00:18:31,069 --> 00:18:32,528
and let you know
how it went with Joey.

442
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:33,613
You told her?!

443
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:36,449
She pulled it out of me.

444
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:38,492
She's like
a conversational wizard.

445
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:40,494
How did it go?

446
00:18:40,536 --> 00:18:42,705
Well, you were wrong.
He doesn't like me.

447
00:18:42,747 --> 00:18:44,373
What?
Yeah.

448
00:18:44,415 --> 00:18:46,459
How would you like it if
I sent you to Lee Majors' house

449
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:47,919
and I told you
that he liked you

450
00:18:47,961 --> 00:18:49,587
and you went down there,
and you found out

451
00:18:49,629 --> 00:18:51,547
that he didn't like you--
how would you feel?

452
00:18:55,175 --> 00:18:57,095
I don't think I'd care.

453
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:59,138
Really? Lee Majors is hot.

454
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:02,475
JOEY:
Hello?

455
00:19:02,516 --> 00:19:04,685
We're in the bathroom.

456
00:19:04,727 --> 00:19:06,186
Why?

457
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:09,565
Because it's a relaxing
and enjoyable time.

458
00:19:12,068 --> 00:19:13,653
What are guys doing in here?

459
00:19:13,694 --> 00:19:15,738
Oh, my God.

460
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:19,158
A friend he's looking
at differently

461
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:21,995
but it's wrong...
it's Rachel.

462
00:19:22,036 --> 00:19:23,203
You like Rachel?!

463
00:19:23,245 --> 00:19:24,789
Look, it's no big deal, okay?

464
00:19:24,831 --> 00:19:26,373
Phoebe and I talked about it.

465
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:28,334
It's just a crush.
It's going to go away.

466
00:19:28,375 --> 00:19:30,544
Dude, you got to rearrange
your bubbles. Whoa.

467
00:19:32,588 --> 00:19:34,465
Mazel tov.

468
00:19:34,507 --> 00:19:35,800
Yeah.

469
00:19:35,842 --> 00:19:37,135
Hey. Ooh... Hi.

470
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:38,511
Hey.
Hey.

471
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:40,763
Ross and I were
looking for you.

472
00:19:40,805 --> 00:19:43,599
What are we all
doing in here?

473
00:19:43,641 --> 00:19:45,225
Oh, my.

474
00:19:45,267 --> 00:19:48,479
Honey, cover it
up with the boat.

475
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:52,025
ROSS:
Hello?

476
00:19:52,066 --> 00:19:56,112
Yes, we're all in here, and
we'd love for you to join us.

477
00:19:56,154 --> 00:19:57,864
Hi.

478
00:19:57,905 --> 00:19:59,032
Well, hey...

479
00:19:59,073 --> 00:20:01,200
what's going on?

480
00:20:01,241 --> 00:20:02,994
Ooh, cool boat.

481
00:20:03,036 --> 00:20:04,120
Oh, no.

482
00:20:04,162 --> 00:20:07,373
Hey, did you tell them?

483
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:08,833
No, I was
waiting for you.

484
00:20:08,875 --> 00:20:09,792
Tell us what?

485
00:20:09,834 --> 00:20:11,544
We're having a girl.

486
00:20:11,585 --> 00:20:12,920
Oh, wow! Really?

487
00:20:12,962 --> 00:20:17,717
( all talking excitedly )

488
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:19,343
I'll get you later.

489
00:20:26,433 --> 00:20:31,939
All right, it's a new day, and
it's just a crush, that's all.

490
00:20:31,981 --> 00:20:33,774
Just a little crush.

491
00:20:33,816 --> 00:20:37,444
All that worrying I was doing--
that was crazy... crazy!

492
00:20:37,486 --> 00:20:39,530
Like my friend the bird here
would say

493
00:20:39,572 --> 00:20:41,574
"It was cuckoo."

494
00:20:45,285 --> 00:20:47,371
Everything's going to be fine.

495
00:20:47,413 --> 00:20:49,207
It's just a crush.

496
00:20:50,791 --> 00:20:51,918
Hi, sweetie.

497
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:53,544
I love you.

498
00:21:02,595 --> 00:21:04,555
It's nice to do this
together, isn't it?

499
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:07,850
Yeah.

500
00:21:07,892 --> 00:21:10,352
And what you're doing
feels so good.

501
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:12,521
I'm not touching you.

502
00:21:12,563 --> 00:21:14,440
You're not?

503
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:16,025
It's the salts.

504
00:21:16,067 --> 00:21:19,612
Oh, sweet Lord,
new realms of pleasure.

505
00:21:19,653 --> 00:21:23,157
Whatever keeps you
off the balcony, big guy.

506
